A||||18||Red2m4||a few odd questions||||6||
Z||000000||Red2m4||07-11-2000||01:28 AM||||Where do i start, well...<P>1.) I have the factory radio w/ cassete.  There is a button that says DNR, what does this do?<P>2.) How hard would it be to wire the head lights so that they move up and down independently?  This way I could "wink" at girls and "salute" other fiero owners.  Would people even know what the hell this meant?<P>3.) I'm thinking about getting an alarm, remote lock and maybe a remote start system.  Are these a pain in the butt to install?  Should I let the seller do it?<P>4.)  Would it be possible to fabricate some sort of split rear window that opens?  Kinda like in a pick up truck?  Or maybe make the window out of plastic, so it could be removed, and maybe stored in the trunk?  Saw a civic DelSol the other day, got me thinkin.<P> <P>||||reg||6
Z||000001||StuGood||07-11-2000||01:49 AM||||DNR = don't (k)now, really.  Or, Department of Natural Resources, etc.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Actually, think it stands for "Dynamic Noise Reduction," which (I guess) is supposed to be some kind of "Delco Dolby," but costs less and doesn't infringe on anyone's patents.  I really don't know what it does - but if you turn it off, there seems to be more noise in the background.  Of the radio, that is  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.<P>Winky lights?  Glad you asked  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">! I've got a nice, simple, cheap circuit installed on my 1987 GT that winks the left headlight (headlight goes up, light winks on and off a couple times, headlight comes down), to salute other Fieros on the highway.<P>I designed the circuit so that you can operate it from a little switch next to the dimmer dial.  And it's dirt-simple to wire; you don't have to run any wires through firewall.  It talks through the existing wire harness.<P>Remote starters have probably been installed on these cars.  Try doing a search through the archives.<P>Split rear window sounds fairly ambitious to me.  Maybe I'll think about it after someone else does it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.          ||||reg||10
Z||000002||Patrick||07-11-2000||01:53 AM||||<BR>I'll take a crack at number one.<P>DNR - Dynamic Noise Reduction. Supposed to help reduce tape hiss during playback. Maybe so, but it usually also reduces other high frequency sounds that you DO want to hear. Use at your own discretion.||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||07-11-2000||01:55 AM||||Gee, I thought it stood for "Do Not Remove" -- I did anyway -- replaced it with a Delco AM/FM/CD w/ 7-band graphic equalizer out of a '98 Grand Am........well, enough about that........<P>Stugood!! Winky lights!! I love it -- how much would you charge me to make up another little circuit board and include instructions?? That is one of the coolest ideas yet!! email me at  <A HREF="mailto:terry@tgowens">terry@tgowens</A>  and let me know!!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/my_fiero_sig.gif">   <BR>'87 Fiero GT -  <A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||07-11-2000||02:23 AM||||there's a vacuum created behind the rear glass that sucks hot air out of the engine compartment.. would a del-sol type window there affect this at all?<P>and wouldn't it make the cabin rather noisy?<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||07-11-2000||03:01 AM||||Putting in an alarm system/remote starter is better to do it yourself. Most places just tape the brainbox under the dash and use "Qwik-Klips" to attach/splice wires. <BR>My Alarm system has the Brainbox hidden and all wires are soldered and sleeved. Never had a problem. <BR>The harder it is for the theif to find the brainbox the harder the car is to steal. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||redfiero||07-11-2000||06:36 AM||||I always thought DNR was Dolby Noise Reduction!||||reg||1
Z||000007||stimpy||07-11-2000||06:45 AM||||Re: the remote star, you do have an automatic, correct? Remote start will not work on a manual transmission.||||reg||1
Z||000008||terryk||07-11-2000||11:45 AM||||Oh, it will work on a manual, it just has other problems, such as driving itself.||||reg||12
Z||000009||Megafiero||07-11-2000||12:01 PM||||If you have a manual trans,  a remote started can still work.  You just have to put a jumper on it so that it can not tell if the clutch is pushed in, then leave it in N, and set the parking break.||||reg||1
Z||000010||theogre||07-12-2000||12:44 PM||||DNR is not Dolby. it's a clone. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Ironhorse||07-12-2000||02:19 PM||||about the rear window that has door open like truck split glass whatever you call it.. I would think to get a med or full size truck rear window that has this already and take it to the shop that will cut it according to the orginal fiero glass size and just mount it on.  oh man.. now you really got me thinkin Red2m4 *chuckle*  that's the path I would take if I was gonna do it.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Raydar||07-12-2000||03:44 PM||||I dunno about the rear window... I understand that it is actually part of the structure of the space frame. Meaning that if it is replaced, the car might flex excessively. Might even crack a thinner window. I would ask Ed Parks, or whoever your resident expert is. (Anybody?)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||StuGood||07-14-2000||01:09 AM||||tgowens:<BR> - Tried to e-mail you several times with addditional information on the "Winky Light," but each time received a message that the server was down.  If you are still interested, please e-mail me.<P>Thanks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.||||reg||9
Z||000014||WKDFIRO||07-14-2000||02:41 AM||||Fiero Motorsports had an F-40 rebody come in for some suspension work. He had accidently put a wrench through the rear window earlier while he was working on the engine. He plexiglassed it, SLATHERED the thing with black goo and kept having to deal with cracking plexiglass. I do know the windshield is a part of the chassis and if the back window is also I wouldn't doubt it. At a scrap yard we saw a crane droping an old chassis with the rear window intact dropping it on the ground B pillar first from less then 10 feet. THE WINDOW DID'T BREAK! Made me feel safe about that B-pillar! <P>Another thing that could be sucked in through a rear window besides hot air is ANY exhaust leaks! Del Sols don't have this potential problem since the engine is in the front. <P>Hmmmm....I feel sleepy....||||reg||4
Z||000015||rogergarrison||07-14-2000||03:20 PM||||if you were to remove, or put an opening rear window a lot of bad things will happen.<BR>1/ its going to suck in all those nasty fumes and put you to sleep permanently.<BR>2/ its going to roast the back of you and your passengers head.<BR> <BR>replacing it with plexiglas will get you a big gob of clear tinted plastic goo on the front of your engine.<P>at high speed with my sunroof popped open it even sucks in fumes. I have to remove the sunroof or keep it closed unless im driving in town.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Formula||07-14-2000||07:36 PM||||I thought the convertable kits didnt have a rear window?  ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Majik||07-14-2000||07:49 PM||||About the back window...speaking from expierence:  I had mine busted out in a robbery (at 7-11)...drove around with it out, and let me tell you, I had it replaced today, and I feel that is the most valuable part of the car.  Not only does all of the hot air come into the car (unless you have the windows up/ac on), but the engine is rather loud (expecially on the interstate).  If there were a way to seal off the engine compartment around that area, it could work, but then again, you probally wouldn't want to do that.  Just IMHO.<P>Majik<BR>Glad to have the quiet cabin again!!!||||reg||1
Z||000018||StuGood||07-15-2000||01:02 PM||||That'll teach you to try and use your Fiero to rob a 7-11  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> !  (Just kidding)<P>BTW, I learned something here.  Before I read this, if anyone had told me the glass was structural, I wouldn't have believed it.  Thanks for the info.    ||||reg||12
